  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordinated lifesaving multisectoral response to crisis affected populations in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an emergency rapid response led by the Norwegian Refugee Council that coordinates lifesaving multisector response to affected communities in
hard-to-reach areas or areas with low presence of humanitarian actors, guided by the emergency rapid response mechanism (ERRM) Framework mainly in Upper Nile and Northern Jonglei. It will have a static presence in 6 out of 10 States plus Pibor and Ruweng Administrative Areas.</narrative>
  </description>
